1|// Fused grouped experts kernel: direction (a), ONE Metal kernel, no sort/unsort.
2|//
3|// Threadgroup e (0..59, 192 threads) serves every (row, slot) pair routed to
4|// expert e, in chunks of 2 pairs. Gate/up/down plus silu-mul are fused with
5|// gate/up/hidden intermediates on-chip (no hidden DRAM round-trip).
6|//
7|// Numerics follow attempt-3's G2-proven forms exactly (same values, same
8|// order): per product, weight/scales/x tiles stream through threadgroup
9|// memory while each thread accumulates with even/odd-K split accumulators
10|// and plain s*(shifted nibble)+bias dequant, rounding (bfloat)(even+odd);
11|// silu is MLX's stable bfloat form verbatim. Gate/up match attempt-3 k1
12|// thread-for-thread (2 pairs x 2 outputs); down matches k2's per-thread
13|// shape (2 pairs x 2 outputs, 8 accs) over 2 output blocks, keeping
14|// occupancy parity. Valid for every row count 1..32 (grid rows-independent;
15|// rows from x_shape[0]; all indexing in bounds; phantom slots valid, stores
16|// guarded).
17|using namespace metal;
18|
